{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Wicked Game feels like a natural next choice if it is the Il Divo album, because I have already chosen several of their releases and want more of that expressive singing.",
    "Forte, if it is the vocal ensemble album I recognize, and Songs From The Silver Screen appeal to my interest in polished crossover vocals and songs like those on Stages."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect to things I have listened to before, but I want music for everyday listening right now.",
    "Enjoying Downton Abbey music does not mean I want every soundtrack; Frozen does not give me the same reason to listen.",
    "Titles like 25 and Hope leave me unsure whether the music offers the expressive vocals or relaxing sound I am looking for."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference regardless of my current mood.",
    "My interest in a particular television soundtrack seems to have been stretched into a broader interest in soundtracks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of Il Divo releases suggest that familiar voices and their style of singing matter to me.",
    "My latest choice of relaxing classical music suggests that calm everyday listening deserves more attention alongside my interest in expressive vocals."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in expressive crossover singing, but leaned too heavily on past holiday listening and broad soundtrack connections."
}"}
